t":"IUT / BUT (university institute of technology)","university":"University","engineering_school":"Engineering school","other":"Other"}},"whatsNew":{"title":"What's new in Studomate {version}","previous":"Previous","next":"Next","done":"Got it","slides":{"offline":{"title":"Studomate works offline","body":"Once the app has loaded, you can keep designing and simulating your projects without a network. A message tells you when an update is available."},"scene3d":{"title":"3D scenes for your simulations","body":"Attach a 3D scene to your project and watch the physical process react to your program, on top of the HMI pages."}}}},"now":"$undefined","timeZone":"UTC","children":["$L1a","$L1b"]}]
18:["$","$L19",null,{"formats":"$undefined","locale":"en","messages":{"public":{"landing":{"heroTitle":"Learn GRAFCET and Ladder<br></br>by simulating them","heroTagline":"Design, simulate and test your automation logic with animated HMIs, right in your browser.","heroBadges":"Free and open source · No install · No account · No personal data","heroSceneLabel":"3D animation of a box-sorting station: a conveyor brings each box and cylinders sort it by height.","followTraining":"Take the course","showcaseGrafcetAlt":"The Studomate editor simulating a GRAFCET","showcaseLadderAlt":"The Studomate editor simulating a Ladder diagram","showcaseHmiAlt":"The Studomate HMI editor","demoTitle":"See Studomate in action","demoVideoLabel":"Demo of building and simulating a project with Studomate","demoVideoPause":"Pause the demo","demoVideoPlay":"Play the demo","logicTitle":"Write the logic","logicIntro":"GRAFCET and Ladder in the same project, sharing the same variables.","machineTitle":"Drive the machine","machineIntro":"Connect your program to an HMI, a 3D scene or a real Arduino board.","showcaseGrafcetTitle":"GRAFCET","showcaseGrafcetText":"Draw steps, transitions and branches, then follow the GRAFCET as it runs: active steps, true conditions, running actions.","showcaseLadderTitle":"Ladder","showcaseLadderText":"Build rungs with contacts, coils, timers and counters, and watch power flow through them during simulation.","showcaseHmiTitle":"HMI","showcaseHmiText":"Build animated supervision pages (lights, buttons, tanks, moving objects) wired to the same variables as your programs.","showcaseScene3dTitle":"3D scenes","showcaseScene3dText":"Connect your program to a virtual 3D plant (conveyors, cylinders, sensors) and watch the machine respond in real time.","showcaseScene3dAlt":"3D scene of a box-sorting station driven by Studomate","showcaseArduinoTitle":"Arduino","showcaseArduinoText":"Load your program onto a real Arduino Uno R3 board, or use its inputs and outputs during simulation, straight from Chrome or Edge.","showcaseArduinoAlt":"Arduino Uno R3 board","whyTitle":"Why Studomate?","whyIntro":"Studomate exists to cut the friction of learning automation down to almost nothing.","reasonFrictionTitle":"Zero friction","reasonFrictionText":"No install, no licence, no PLC or I/O cards to set up. You focus on the logic, not the tool.","reasonAllInOneTitle":"All-in-one","reasonAllInOneText":"GRAFCET, Ladder and animated HMIs in the same environment, with variables shared across all three. No free tool combines the three.","reasonShortLoopTitle":"Short correction loop","reasonShortLoopText":"Errors are flagged while you edit, not only when you start the simulation. A fast, visual right to make mistakes.","audienceStudents":"Students (technical colleges, engineering schools, universities)","audienceTeachers":"Teachers and trainers in automation / electrical engineering","audienceProfessionals":"Professionals retraining or brushing up","featureSimulationTitle":"Real-time simulation","featureSimulationText":"Step-by-step or continuous execution, with live visualisation of states, transitions and variables.","featureManualTitle":"Built-in manual","featureManualText":"Complete help available straight from the app.","featureCloudTitle":"Accounts & cloud (optional)","featureCloudText":"Projects stored locally or in the cloud, with link sharing.","stepsTitle":"Get started in 30 seconds","step1Title":"Open the app","step1Text":"Nothing to install — it all runs in the browser.","step2Title":"Create a project or start from an example","step2Text":"Start from scratch or open one of the ready-made templates.","step3Title":"Analyse, then simulate","step3Text":"Check the structure, then run the logic and watch the system react.","trainingTitle":"Learn industrial automation with Studomate","trainingIntro":"Guided modules to master GRAFCET, then Ladder, with exercises you can simulate in the app.","trainingA0Topic":"Basics","trainingA0Summary":"Automation, variables, basic logic and the scan cycle.","trainingA1Topic":"GRAFCET","trainingA1Summary":"Steps, transitions, actions, OR and AND branches.","trainingA2Topic":"Ladder","trainingA2Summary":"Contacts, coils, latching, set/reset coils and edges.","trainingA3Topic":"Ladder","trainingA3Summary":"Timers, counters, calculations and subroutines.","trainingA4Topic":"GRAFCET → Ladder","trainingA4Summary":"Implement a GRAFCET in Ladder: one network per transition, two programs, actions, time and faults.","trainingA5Topic":"GRAFCET → Ladder (continued)","trainingA5Summary":"OR and AND divergences, stopping a sequence, limits of one network per transition and the three-block method.","trainingCta":"Browse all training","templatesTitle":"Examples to get you started","templatesIntro":"Open a pre-configured project and explore it at your own pace.","templatePreviewAlt":"Preview of the {label} project","openInApp":"Open in the app","durabilityTitle":"Your projects are yours","durabilityNoLockInTitle":"No lock-in","durabilityNoLockInText":"Your projects are files you export and keep. The schema is versioned: a project exported today will still open after the tool is updated.","durabilityIndependenceTitle":"You depend on no one","durabilityIndependenceText":"The code is free under the AGPL v3 licence: if the project stops, it can be forked or self-hosted.","privacyTitle":"Built for privacy","privacyText":"No email required, no personal data stored, no tracking cookies. Authentication uses a nickname, and usage statistics are anonymous.","sourceCodeText":"The source code is public: read it, report an issue or contribute.","viewOnGitHub":"View on GitHub","openApp":"Open the app"},"metadata":{"homeTitle":"Studomate: Online GRAFCET and Ladder Simulator","homeDescription":"Design and simulate GRAFCET, Ladder and animated HMIs in the same browser: no install, no account.","aboutTitle":"About","aboutDescription":"Studomate: a free teaching tool to learn, design and simulate GRAFCET, Ladder and HMIs in the browser.","contactTitle":"Contact","contactDescription":"Contact the Studomate team: ideas, feedback, contributions.","legalTitle":"Legal notice","legalDescription":"Legal notice for the Studomate site.","termsTitle":"Terms of use","termsDescription":"Terms of use for Studomate.","privacyTitle":"Privacy policy","privacyDescription":"How Studomate handles users' personal and technical data.","manualTitle":"User manual","manualDescription":"Studomate user manual: getting started, GRAFCET, Ladder, HMI, simulation.","trainingTitle":"Free GRAFCET and Ladder training","trainingDescription":"Automation control training path with Studomate: theory, self-corrected exercises, summary assignments.","glossaryTitle":"Automation glossary: GRAFCET and Ladder","glossaryDescription":"Automation glossary: step, transition, contact, coil, TON, counter, edge... every GRAFCET and Ladder term defined simply, with diagrams.","trainingA0Title":"Module A0: Before you start","trainingA0Description":"Module A0: what an automated system is, variables and basic logic, the scan cycle. The prerequisites before GRAFCET.","trainingA1Title":"Module A1: GRAFCET basics","trainingA1Description":"Module A1: steps, transitions, receptivities, actions, OR and AND divergences. Theory and self-corrected exercises.","trainingA2Title":"Module A2: Ladder, logic and memory","trainingA2Description":"Module A2: from the relay diagram to Ladder, contacts and coils, self-holding, S/R coils, edges and network execution order.","trainingA3Title":"Module A3: Ladder, time and calculation","trainingA3Description":"Module A3: timers, counters, calculation and numeric types, subprograms: theory and self-corrected exercises.","trainingA4Title":"Module A4: From GRAFCET to Ladder (part 1)","trainingA4Description":"Module A4: implementing a GRAFCET in Ladder, from step to outputs: one network per transition, two programs, actions, timers and faults.","trainingA5Title":"Module A5: From GRAFCET to Ladder (part 2)","trainingA5Description":"Module A5: OR and AND divergences, stopping a sequence, limits of one network per transition and the three-block method for a GRAFCET in Ladder.","manualSections":{"getting-started":{"title":"Getting started with Studomate: manual","description":"Create a project, add a GRAFCET or a ladder, define variables and run a first simulation in Studomate."},"projects":{"title":"Studomate projects: user manual","description":"Programs, variables, HMI screens and dialect: what a Studomate project contains, and how to save, open and export it."},"accounts":{"title":"Accounts and sharing: Studomate manual","description":"Cloud backup, sync across devices and sharing a project by link: using a Studomate account."},"explorer":{"title":"Project explorer: Studomate manual","description":"The Studomate explorer: project tree, programs, variables and HMI screens, and the interface panels."},"variables":{"title":"PLC variables: Studomate manual","description":"Areas, mnemonics, types and initial values: declare and manage the variables of a GRAFCET, Ladder and HMI project."},"grafcet":{"title":"GRAFCET editor: Studomate manual","description":"Steps, transitions, actions, junctions, referrals and links: create and edit a GRAFCET in the Studomate graphical editor."},"ladder":{"title":"Ladder editor: Studomate manual","description":"Networks, contacts, coils, blocks and connections: create and edit a Ladder program in the Studomate graphical editor."},"toolbar":{"title":"Toolbar: Studomate manual","description":"General actions and creation tools of the Studomate toolbar, depending on the open program type (GRAFCET or Ladder)."},"cross-references":{"title":"Cross-references: Studomate manual","description":"See where each variable is read and written across the GRAFCETs, ladders and HMI screens of a Studomate project."},"hmi":{"title":"Animated HMI screens: Studomate manual","description":"Pages, widgets, properties, animations and events: design an interactive human-machine interface and drive it in simulation."},"simulation":{"title":"PLC simulation: Studomate manual","description":"Start and stop the simulation, follow variables with watch tables and drive HMI screens in real time."},"analysis":{"title":"Project analysis: Studomate manual","description":"Static analysis checks a project's consistency before simulation: types of checks, blocking errors and warnings."},"hardware":{"title":"Arduino Uno R3: Studomate manual","description":"Load a program onto an Arduino Uno R3 board, use it as the inputs and outputs of a simulation, or observe its program."},"scene3d":{"title":"3D simulation scene: Studomate manual","description":"Link a virtual 3D plant (crate sorting, elevator, traffic lights, drilling) to a program running in simulation."},"limits":{"title":"Tool limits: Studomate manual","description":"What Studomate does not do: limits of Grafcet, expressions, Arduino hardware, 3D scenes and project storage."},"troubleshooting":{"title":"Troubleshooting: Studomate manual","description":"What to do when the simulation will not start, the grafcet stays stuck or an input does not respond: common symptoms and their causes."},"shortcuts":{"title":"Keyboard shortcuts: Studomate manual","description":"All Studomate keyboard shortcuts for Windows, Linux and macOS: editing, simulation, navigation and export."}},"trainingStepFallbackTitle":"{step} (module {module}, Studomate Training)","trainingSteps":{"a0":{"logic-basics":{"title":"Variables and basic logic in automation: training","description":"Boolean variables, true and false states, AND, OR, NOT: the logic basics to know before programming a PLC."},"scan-cycle":{"title":"The PLC and its scan cycle: training","description":"How a programmable controller runs its program in a loop: the scan cycle, illustrated with a traffic light."},"conclusion":{"title":"Module A0 conclusion: automation basics","description":"Module A0 recap: sensors, actuators, PLC, variables, AND/OR/NOT logic and the scan cycle, then what comes next with GRAFCET."}},"a1":{"theory":{"title":"GRAFCET steps, transitions and receptivities: training","description":"Active or inactive step, transition, receptivity and action: the basic elements of a GRAFCET, with examples in Studomate."},"theory-actions":{"title":"GRAFCET action types and execution modes: training","description":"Actions on boolean or numeric variables and the execution modes of a GRAFCET's actions."},"theory-timer":{"title":"Timing a GRAFCET receptivity: training","description":"Make a receptivity depend on the time spent in a step, following the IEC 60848 standard: notation and examples."},"theory-or-divergence":{"title":"GRAFCET OR divergence and convergence: training","description":"Choose between several sequences: OR divergence and convergence in a GRAFCET, with examples."},"theory-and-divergence":{"title":"GRAFCET AND divergence and convergence: training","description":"Start several branches in parallel and resynchronise them: AND divergence and convergence in a GRAFCET, with examples."},"reading-errors":{"title":"Reading GRAFCET analysis errors: training","description":"Analyze a GRAFCET without simulating it and understand Studomate's errors and warnings to fix your program."}},"a2":{"theory-contacts-coils":{"title":"Contacts, coils and internal memories in Ladder: training","description":"Ladder symbols: NO and NC contacts, normally open or normally closed button wiring, coils and internal memories."},"theory-self-holding":{"title":"Self-holding in Ladder: training","description":"Remember a short push of a push button: the self-holding circuit in Ladder, with a pump example."},"theory-set-reset":{"title":"Set and Reset coils in Ladder: training","description":"S (set) and R (reset) coils: remember a state without self-holding and understand the execution order of networks."},"theory-edges":{"title":"Rising and falling edges in Ladder: training","description":"P and N edge contacts: trigger an action only once per push, with rising and falling edges."},"conclusion":{"title":"Module A2 conclusion: Ladder logic","description":"Module A2 recap: combinational logic, memory, self-holding, S/R coils and edges in Ladder, and what comes next."}},"a3":{"theory-counters":{"title":"CTU, CTD and CTUD counters in Ladder: training","description":"Count parts or cycles with CTU, CTD and CTUD counters: how the blocks work, with examples in Studomate."},"theory-numeric":{"title":"Processing numeric values in Ladder: training","description":"Assignment, calculations and comparisons: process a level, a counter or a setpoint in a Ladder program."},"theory-types":{"title":"INT, DINT, REAL types and conversions in Ladder: training","description":"The INT, DINT, REAL, WORD and DWORD numeric types, and conversions between types in a Ladder program."},"theory-structure":{"title":"Structuring a Ladder program into subprograms: training","description":"Split a Ladder program into subprograms: the Main program calls one subprogram per machine function, so each part stays readable."},"conclusion":{"title":"Module A3 conclusion: Studomate and the standard","description":"Module A3 recap: timers, counters, numeric values and how to structure a Ladder program into subprograms."}},"a4":{"theory-method-ladder":{"title":"From GRAFCET to Ladder: one network per transition","description":"Implement a GRAFCET in Ladder: one network per transition (upstream reset, downstream set), order of the networks and activation of the initial step."},"theory-two-programs":{"title":"Two Ladder programs for a GRAFCET: training","description":"Arrange a GRAFCET implemented in Ladder into two programs, Automatic_cycle and Outputs, called by the Main: a complete example and a checklist."},"theory-actions-ladder":{"title":"Continuous and stored actions in Ladder: training","description":"Implement a GRAFCET's continuous, stored and conditional actions in Ladder: one network per output, in the Outputs program."},"theory-edge-actions-ladder":{"title":"Edge and numeric actions in Ladder: training","description":"Implement a GRAFCET's edge actions in Ladder with P and N contacts, and numeric assignments, on a car-counting example."},"theory-receptivity-timer":{"title":"A delay in a receptivity in Ladder: training","description":"Place the TON of a receptivity delay in the transition's network, and delay or limit an output with a step and a timed transition."},"theory-movement-supervision":{"title":"Supervising a movement in Ladder: training","description":"Supervise a movement with a TON and a fallback transition, latch the fault in the Faults program and acknowledge it without clearing it if the cause persists."},"conclusion":{"title":"Module A4 conclusion: GRAFCET in Ladder, part 1","description":"Module A4 recap: steps as memories, network per transition, Automatic_cycle and Outputs programs, actions, time and faults of a GRAFCET implemented in Ladder."}},"a5":{"theory-and-divergence-ladder":{"title":"AND divergence and convergence in Ladder: training","description":"Implement a GRAFCET's AND divergence and convergence in Ladder: a single network for the divergence and a single one for the convergence."},"theory-grafcet-reset":{"title":"Stopping a GRAFCET sequence in Ladder: training","description":"The two ways of stopping a sequence in Ladder: immediate stop by reinitialisation and end-of-cycle stop, and where to place the reset network."},"theory-going-further":{"title":"Limits of one network per transition: training","description":"When one network per transition reaches its limit (one press read by several transitions), on a single-button remote gate example."},"theory-three-blocks":{"title":"The three-block method in Ladder: training","description":"The three-block method to implement a GRAFCET in Ladder: crossing conditions, all the resets then all the sets, then the outputs."},"conclusion":{"title":"Module A5 conclusion: GRAFCET in Ladder, part 2","description":"Module A5 recap: OR and AND divergences, stopping a sequence, the car park's programs and the limits of one network per transition."}}}}},"templates":{"traffic-light":{"label":"Traffic light","description":"3 boolean outputs (red, amber, green) + an HMI with coloured indicators. To be programmed."},"crossroads":{"label":"Traffic light crossroads","description":"12 boolean outputs (red/amber/green × 4 lights: NS1, NS2, EO1, EO2) + an HMI with the crossroads. Plant simulated by the 3D scene. To be programmed."},"drilling":{"label":"Drilling station","description":"Sequential cycle driven by limit switches: start button, lowering, timed drilling, raising. Console and plant simulated by the 3D scene. To be programmed."},"elevator":{"label":"Lift","description":"3-floor lift: landing and car buttons, floor display and lamps in the 3D scene that simulates the plant. To be programmed."},"parking":{"label":"Barrier car park","description":"Two barriers (entry and exit) and a space counter: sensors for a waiting car, a photocell under the barrier, a \"full\" lamp and a counter in the 3D scene, where the Arrival and Departure buttons bring cars. To be programmed."},"carton-sorting":{"label":"Carton sorting station","description":"Sorting cartons by height: detection at the post, routing by three cylinders to two output conveyors, counting. Plant simulated by the 3D scene. To be programmed."},"linear-sequence":{"label":"Linear sequence","description":"A 4-step GRAFCET, a single chain, no timer or divergence. Training module mini-exercise."},"and-divergence":{"label":"AND divergence","description":"An AND divergence closed by its convergence, two parallel branches. Training module mini-exercise."},"or-divergence":{"label":"OR divergence","description":"A two-branch OR divergence with mutually exclusive branches, each looping back to the initial state on its own. Training module mini-exercise."},"timer-cycle":{"label":"Timer","description":"A 2-step GRAFCET alternating on two timers, no input. Training module observation."},"ladder-and-or":{"label":"Series and parallel contacts","description":"Two networks provided: toggle a and b in simulation to observe AND and OR. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-reading":{"label":"Read a Ladder program","description":"Four combinational networks provided: predict the outputs, then check in simulation. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-logic":{"label":"Two-way lighting","description":"Combinational logic: two switches and an enable. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-self-holding":{"label":"Pump: self-holding","description":"Push-button start, stop priority, self-holding. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-interlock":{"label":"Reversing motor","description":"Two interlocked self-holdings with a common stop. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-memory":{"label":"Pump: latched fault","description":"Thermal relay, latched fault lamp, acknowledgement without automatic restart. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-edges-reading":{"label":"Read edges","description":"The same input on a NO, P and N contact: record the timing diagram. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-toggle":{"label":"Impulse relay","description":"One button turns a lamp on then off: network execution order and P contact. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-gate":{"label":"Motorised gate","description":"Two interlocked directions, limit switches, stop, photocell. The student declares the inputs. Training module synthesis."},"ladder-timers-reading":{"label":"Read timers","description":"A TON, a TOF and a TP on the same input: draw the timing diagrams. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-timers":{"label":"Star-delta start","description":"Star then delta with a TON, fan held by a TOF, two-TON blinker. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-counters":{"label":"Counting","description":"Piece counting (CTU), buffer zone (CTUD), stock (CTD). Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-tank":{"label":"Tank","description":"Level hysteresis, alarm, start counter on a P contact. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-scaling":{"label":"Scaling","description":"Computing a level from a raw value: overflow, truncation, REAL computation. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-subprograms":{"label":"Subprograms","description":"Call the counting subprogram from the Main, and see the effect of a conditional call. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-packing":{"label":"Case packing","description":"Conveyor, fault, counting and box change in subprograms. No variables provided. Training module synthesis."},"linear-sequence-naive-ladder":{"label":"Linear sequence: textbook method","description":"Linear GRAFCET implemented with one self-holding per step: observe the overlap. Training module mini-exercise."},"linear-sequence-ladder":{"label":"Linear sequence in Ladder","description":"Implement a linear GRAFCET in Ladder, one network per transition. Training module mini-exercise."},"drilling-ladder":{"label":"Drilling station in Ladder","description":"Drilling GRAFCET in Ladder, timer and descent watchdog. Training module synthesis."},"or-divergence-ladder":{"label":"OR divergence in Ladder","description":"An OR divergence implemented in Ladder. Training module mini-exercise."},"and-divergence-ladder":{"label":"AND divergence in Ladder","description":"An AND divergence implemented in Ladder. Training module mini-exercise."},"traffic-light-ladder":{"label":"Traffic light in Ladder","description":"Traffic light in Ladder with reset and end-of-cycle stop. Training module mini-exercise."},"parking-ladder":{"label":"Parking in Ladder","description":"Parking control in Ladder, signalling provided, reset. Training module synthesis."},"gate-per-transition-ladder":{"label":"Remote-controlled gate: one network per transition","description":"Single-button gate implemented with one network per transition. Training module example."},"gate-grafcet-ladder":{"label":"Remote-controlled gate: three blocks","description":"Single-button gate implemented in three blocks. Training module example."}}},"now":"$undefined","timeZone":"UTC","children":"$L1c"}]
